.TH CBMAP_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_reset \- clear all elements from the map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_reset(cbmap cbm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes all the key-value pairs from the map, which becomes empty but
stays usable by the caller.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm  BST map to reset
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns ccol_success on success
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(n) complexity
The function destroys all the nodes and frees the keys and the values
The function asserts if cbm is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_destroy (3),
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3)
